WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.723
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:06.840
- [Narrator] In 2010, "Tron: Legacy"

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.410
became the first sequel to be released

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:10.640
more than 20 years after its predecessor

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.810
as Jeff Bridges had to wait 28 years

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:14.320
to return to The Grid.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.440
A rash of franchises were
dusted off from 2015 onward,

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:18.810
with "Mad Max: Fury Road"

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.997
releasing 29 years after
"Beyond Thunderdome,"

00:00:21.997 --> 00:00:24.510
"Blade Runner 2049" dropping 35 years

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.920
after "Blade Runner,"
"Mary Poppins Returns"

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.420
landing 54 years after
"Mary Poppins" in 2018,

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.490
and "Doctor Sleep" coming 39 years

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:35.040
after "The Shining" in 2019.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.050
But, unlike the aforementioned films,

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.940
Tron's cult following of self-described

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:41.820
users has also been a little more niche,

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.960
which is why it's taken more than a decade

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.850
to receive any substantial news

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:47.710
on a third "Tron" film.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:49.660
The fact that "Tron" had
the longest-sequel gap

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.290
is appropriate for Tron's
unique space in fandom,

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:53.810
it's a franchise that's always ahead

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:55.360
of the technological curve

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.800
and it always understands
the power of nostalgia

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:00.200
when it comes to blockbuster film making.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.180
- Hey, who's that guy?

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:04.880
- That's Tron, he fights for the users.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.130
- [Narrator] Even so,
"Tron" is always fighting

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.680
to be taken seriously.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:10.990
- Did anyone see the movie Tron?

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:12.080
- No.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:12.913
- No.

00:01:12.913 --> 00:01:13.746
- No.

00:01:13.746 --> 00:01:14.579
- No.

00:01:14.579 --> 00:01:15.412
- [Narrator] While the franchise

00:01:15.412 --> 00:01:17.120
is always going through fits and starts,

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.520
there does appear to be a flicker

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:20.770
on The Grid in 2020
with news of Jared Leto

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:22.440
confirming a third "Tron" movie

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:24.860
to be directed by Garth Davis.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:27.530
So on the 10 year
anniversary of "Tron: Legacy"

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:29.920
join us as we look back
at the complete franchise

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.710
from its start as one of
the earliest CGI-heavy films

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:35.040
through new reports on the third film.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.610
Who knows, by the end of this video

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:37.740
you might be looking up

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.680
how to make your own Tron costume.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.557
They're actually really cool.

00:01:41.557 --> 00:01:42.730
"Tron" came from the mind

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:45.960
of writer-director and
animator, Steven Lisberger.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.217
Lisberger's first film,

00:01:47.217 --> 00:01:48.750
"Animalympics," was a two-part

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.500
animated TV special commissioned by NBC

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:53.600
to spoof the Winter and Summer Olympics

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.580
as promo for the actual
1980 Moscow Olympics.

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:59.660
However, the US ended up boycotting

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:00.940
the Summer Olympics that year

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:03.210
after Russia invaded Afghanistan

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:05.850
and the Summer special
never aired as intended.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.880
The combined movie did, however, receive

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:09.737
a small theatrical release.

00:02:09.737 --> 00:02:11.240
"Animalympics" is noteworthy

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:13.040
because many involved went on

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:15.230
to make major films for Disney.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.420
For example, Art Director Roger Allers

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:19.420
becoming co-director of "The Lion King,"

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:21.347
animator Brad Bird went on to make

00:02:21.347 --> 00:02:23.580
"The Incredibles 1 and 2,"

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:25.560
but it was Lisberger who first landed

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:28.870
at the mouse house after
"Animalympics," with "Tron."

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:30.950
Though Lisberger initially
conceived of Tron

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.440
as an animated film,

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:33.730
Disney green-lit the project

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:35.940
based on a test reel done by Lisberger

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:39.130
that combined live-action
with computer animation.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:41.780
The concept of virtual
reality as a film's setting,

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:43.970
thus combining live-action with CGI,

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:45.280
was novel at the time,

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:47.120
offering a glimpse into the future

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:50.290
of wholly computer
animated cinematic worlds.

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:52.680
But because 50 minutes
of the film's runtime

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.717
consisted of backlit
animation on a sound stage,

00:02:55.717 --> 00:02:57.730
"Tron" ultimately only consisted

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:01.800
of 16 total minutes of actual CGI.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.940
Still, many of Disney's own 2D animators

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:06.560
refused to work on "Tron"

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.310
for fear that computer animation

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:10.260
was a threat to their jobs.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:12.670
So the computer-generated look of "Tron"

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:14.940
actually came from outside Disney,

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:16.670
utilizing "Alien" and "Blade Runner"

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:18.110
concept artist Syd Mead

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:21.110
and renowned "Heavy Metal"
artist Jean Moebius Giraud

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:23.200
to design the looks of the costumes,

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.180
sets, and storyboards.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.780
Though "Tron" was revolutionary

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:28.290
in regards to special effects

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.290
it was made with just one computer

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.740
with only two megabytes of memory.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:36.070
You likely have more
storage on your cell phone.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.610
The sets were covered top
to bottom in black felt,

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.030
and the colorization of the suits

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:42.900
was actually traditional
hand-drawn animation,

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.140
but the computer-generated sections

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:47.140
kept "Tron" from Oscar consideration

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.170
in visual effects because computers

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:51.557
were considered cheating at the time.

00:03:51.557 --> 00:03:53.300
"Tron" wasn't the box office bomb

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.960
that many frame it as now,

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.620
it just didn't capture audiences

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:59.490
like the new visual
experience expected to.

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:02.060
It earned $33 million at the box office,

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:05.720
making back almost double
its $17 million budget.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:07.690
However, it was its release date

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:10.207
that likely softened its total box office.

00:04:10.207 --> 00:04:12.570
"Tron" was originally
set to open in December

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:14.470
opposite awards hopeful movies

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:17.970
and would've been the only
family options in the winter,

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:19.470
but Disney moved up the release

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:20.960
to the summer out of spite,

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:24.750
hoping to dent the impact
of a former Disney animator.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:27.077
Don Bluth, who worked on
Disney's "Robin Hood,"

00:04:27.077 --> 00:04:29.240
"Pete's Dragon," and "Rescuers Down Under"

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:31.440
had left Disney in 1979

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.770
to start his own animation company.

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:36.390
His first original film
was "The Secret of NIMH,"

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:39.517
set to release in July 1982.

00:04:39.517 --> 00:04:40.910
"Tron" was moved by Disney

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:42.770
to open opposite that film

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:44.100
and while "Tron" did gross

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:45.870
more than double what NIMH did,

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:47.150
it paled in comparison

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:50.040
to other summer
blockbusters of that season.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.737
In the end, "Tron" came
up far behind "E.T.,"

00:04:52.737 --> 00:04:54.817
"Poltergeist," and "Annie" that summer.

00:04:54.817 --> 00:04:56.650
"The Best Little Whorehouse in Texas"

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.970
ended up being the highest
grossing July release of 1982.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:01.640
So while Disney envisioned July

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:03.390
would be "Tron" versus Bluth,

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:06.749
it was good old Dolly
Parton who upended The Grid.

00:05:06.749 --> 00:05:07.582
(Jeff screaming)

00:05:07.582 --> 00:05:09.200
- Fittingly, however, new technology

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.610
at the time afforded a
second life for the film.

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:14.290
As a franchise, "Tron" would benefit

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:17.580
greatly from home video
and the Tron arcade game.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.560
The coin-operated Tron game generated

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:21.840
more revenue than the film itself,

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.330
earning $45 million dollars

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:26.010
from coin playing by 1983.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:27.110
And while a movie sequel

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:29.010
would take 28 years to complete,

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:32.380
the arcade game already
had a sequel in 1983,

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:33.860
the "Discs of Tron,"

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:35.270
which was one of the first games

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.387
to attempt the 3D environment.

00:05:37.387 --> 00:05:38.830
"Discs of Tron" simulated

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:40.520
the jai alai-like combat scenes

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:43.460
between Flynn and Crom and Tron and Sark.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:44.770
These scenes were actually

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:47.280
the genesis of Lisberger's
concept for "Tron"

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:50.720
after seeing the early
Atari computer game "Pong."

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.260
Flying discs for combat
was Lisberger's idea

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:54.830
to have attacks without guns

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:57.090
so that kids wouldn't emulate gunplay,

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:59.870
something that carried
over to the arcade games.

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:01.210
The Tron games were introduced

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:02.800
at the peak of arcade fever

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:05.400
before the 1983 video
game industry crashed

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.120
from over-saturation.

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:08.480
The classic arcade games

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:10.270
would keep the spirit of "Tron" alive

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:12.520
long after the 1982 film

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:14.720
and would also serve as the entry point

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:17.370
for "Tron: Legacy" in 2010.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:19.300
Like the original "Tron," "Tron: Legacy"

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:22.930
went to a first-time live action
filmmaker, Joseph Kosinski.

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:26.070
Kosinski's background was
actually in architecture.

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:28.140
A graduate of architecture at Columbia,

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:30.190
Kosinski specialized in implementing

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:33.120
high-end computer programs
into architecture.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:35.650
This eventually led him
into the commercial world

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:37.580
and directing commercials for video games

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:39.633
which got him noticed by Disney.

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:41.850
- He's different.

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:43.710
- [Narrator] But it was his
architectural background

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:45.260
that informed the design of the film

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:46.900
and the movement within The Grid

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:48.620
that excited fans the most

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:52.680
from the very first teaser
shown at Comic-Con in 2008.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.790
It also made it the most expensive

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:56.440
directorial debut of all time

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:59.210
with a budget of $170 million,

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:01.530
which eventually became $222 million

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:04.233
after applying 3D
conversions and marketing.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:06.537
- it's just a game.

00:07:12.004 --> 00:07:13.980
- Not anymore.

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:15.700
- [Narrator] While
mainstream computer literacy

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:17.630
had skyrocketed in the 28 years

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:18.990
since "Tron" was released,

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:20.930
the filmmakers didn't
wanna fill the script

00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:23.170
with RAM discussions or populate the film

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:26.440
with internal internet ads
and other inside jokes.

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:27.830
Instead, they set out to build

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:30.130
a complete internal world and society

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:31.830
that had advanced organically

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:33.800
in the time between films.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.253
- Disease? History.

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:39.930
Science, philosophy, every idea

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:43.200
man has ever had about
the universe up for grabs.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:45.470
Biodigital jazz, man.

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:47.080
- [Narrator] The sequel,
starring Jeff Bridges

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:48.830
in a dual role, Garrett Hedlund,

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:51.020
Olivia Wilde, and
featuring an original score

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:54.705
by Daft Punk earned $400 million globally.

00:07:54.705 --> 00:07:56.410
(upbeat music)

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:59.220
But because it only barely
made its original budget

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:00.940
back at the domestic box office,

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:04.020
proposed sequels have
languished for a decade.

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:05.160
But like its predecessor,

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:06.540
a cult following has emerged

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:09.220
and fans have begged
for a third "Tron" film.

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:11.770
In 2020, three years
after Kosinski described

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:14.240
a third film as being
in a cryogenic freeze,

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:17.040
the "Tron: Legacy" filmmaker has moved on.

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:18.600
But there is life on The Grid

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:19.960
with filmmaker Garth Davis

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:21.600
winning over Disney with a new pitch

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.990
and actor Jared Leto on board.

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:25.497
Leto says of the projects,

00:08:25.497 --> 00:08:26.980
"I'm struck with such gratitude

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:29.110
for the opportunity to
bring this movie to life,

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:31.090
especially as both the original video game

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:34.490
and the film affected me
so deeply as a young child.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:35.750
The fact that I get to be a part

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:37.920
of this new chapter is mind-blowing."

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:39.470
There is no word on whether Bridges,

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:41.750
Hedlund, or Wilde might return to The Grid

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.470
and insiders stress that the film

00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:45.620
has not officially been green-lit.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.300
However a director being attached

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:48.800
is a step in the right direction

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:51.220
for users to be granted
to The Grid once again,

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:52.920
more than a decade later.

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:55.390
Which iteration of "Tron"
do you love the most?

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:58.150
The original film, the
sequel, or the video games?

00:08:58.150 --> 00:08:59.620
And what do you think the third film

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:00.690
should focus on?

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:03.353
Sound off on the film's
legacy in the comments below.

